>> B2: Describe how file descriptors are associated with open files.
>> Are file descriptors unique within the entire OS or just within a
>> single process?

Each thread has its own fd_table array where each entry points to 
the struct file for that open file using the fd as its index. Fd's are 
not shared (i.e: fd3 in thread A and fd3 in thread B are independent).

Fd's are unique within a thread, not across pintos. So two different 
threads can have the same fd number but they can refer to different 
files.

