>> B10: What advantages or disadvantages can you see to your design
>> for file descriptors?

Advantages:
-> Getting a fie from an fd is an array lookup, so O(1), (i.e: fd_table[fd])
-> Storing the table in a seperate kernel page (using palloc_get_page) keeps struct thread less bloated

Disadvantages:
-> Fd tables have a limit of 64 fd's so it could be too little for programs that open many files


